        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 83-year-old female patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she exhibited increased dyspnea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. She was promptly initiated on supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulized bronchodilators, and a course of systemic corticosteroids. Vital signs were closely monitored throughout her stay. She responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. At discharge, she was stable with satisfactory oxygen saturation on room air. I recommend close outpatient follow-up and review of her inhaler technique and maintenance therapy. Please do not hesitate to contact me with any questions.</div>"
            },
